<h2><code>&lt;date-box&gt;</code></h2>
<p>Stacked day/month/year box. Provide values via named slots; pass <code>datetime</code> (ISO 8601) for machine-readable semantics on the wrapped <code>&lt;time&gt;</code> element.</p>

<date-box datetime="2010-11-05">
  <span slot="day">5</span>
  <span slot="month">November</span>
  <span slot="year">2010</span>
</date-box>

<h2><code>&lt;input&gt;</code></h2>
<p>Forwards all standard HTML input attributes (type, name, value, placeholder, etc.).</p>

<form>
  <input type="text" name="example-text" placeholder="text input">
  <input type="search" name="example-search" placeholder="search input">
  <input type="email" name="example-email" placeholder="email input">
</form>

<h2><code>&lt;submit&gt;</code></h2>
<p>Submit button with themed styling.</p>

<form><submit></submit></form>

<h2><code>&lt;list&gt;</code></h2>
<p>Renders an unordered list from an <code>items</code> array. Use the <code>:</code>
  prefix so the value parses as a JS expression. (Note: the array is also forwarded
  as an HTML attribute on the rendered <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> &mdash; harmless but
  cosmetic.)</p>

<list :items='["First item", "Second item", "Third item"]'></list>

<h2><code>&lt;table-styled&gt;</code></h2>
<p>Data-driven styled table. Pass <code>caption</code> (string), and <code>headers</code>
  / <code>rows</code> arrays with the <code>:</code> expression prefix.</p>

<table-styled
  caption="Recent CSS Specifications"
  :headers='["Spec", "Status", "Year"]'
  :rows='[["CSS 2.1", "REC", "2011"], ["CSS Color 4", "CR", "2022"], ["CSS Cascade 5", "WD", "2024"]]'></table-styled>

<h2><code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code></h2>
<p>Multi-line text input.</p>

<textarea name="example-textarea" rows="3"></textarea>
